<title>UK: Licht sees world 96/97 sugar output at 125.3 mln t.</title>
<headline>Licht sees world 96/97 sugar output at 125.3 mln t.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>World sugar production should reach 125.30 million tonnes raw value in 1996/97, 2.24 million more than in the previous year, statistician F.O. Licht said on Thursday.</p>
<p>In its second estimate of the 1996/97 world output, Licht said its figure was 1.31 million tonnes less than its first estimate released in October but still well in excess of consumption.</p>
<p>The European Union (EU) accounted for most of the expected rise in beet sugar but the cane sector would as usual account for the lion's share of world output with 87.73 million tonnes after 86.65 million in 1995/96.</p>
